    <bpmn:process id="W_W1667" name="W1667. Competitive Intelligence Quarterly Briefing &amp; Strategy Input" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Quarterly competitive intelligence cycle
Frequency: Quarterly
Volume: 1 comprehensive briefing
Owner: CMO
Participants: CMO, VP Merchandising, VP Store Operations, CEO, C-Suite
Source: workflow W1667 — Competitive Intelligence Quarterly Briefing &amp; Strategy Input</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W1667_LaneSet2">
        <bpmn:lane id="W1667_Lane1" name="CMO">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1667_Task4</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1667_Task5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1667_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1667_Start3</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1667_End7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W1667_Start3" name="Quarterly competitive intelligence cycle">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1667_Flow10</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1667_Task4" name="CMO compiles quarterly competitive intelligence briefing from: (a) competitor…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: CMO compiles quarterly competitive intelligence briefing from: (a) competitor store visit data (W1661), (b) market trend analysis (W1662), (c) customer research insights (W1663), (d) pricing intelligence (W1664)
Responsible (R): CMO
Accountable (A): CEO
Duration: 2 days</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1667_Flow10</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1667_Flow11</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1667_Task5" name="Briefing content: (a) competitive landscape summary: new entrants, exits…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Briefing content: (a) competitive landscape summary: new entrants, exits, expansions, format changes, (b) competitor strategy analysis: pricing strategy, assortment strategy, channel strategy, customer acquisition strategy, (c) BuildRight competitive position: market share estimate (where data available), price index trend, customer perception vs. competitors, (d) emerging opportunities and threats, (e) strategic recommendations for BuildRight response
Responsible (R): CMO
Accountable (A): CEO
Duration: —</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1667_Flow11</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1667_Flow12</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1667_Task6" name="CMO presents briefing to CEO and C-Suite: (a) discuss competitive implications…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: CMO presents briefing to CEO and C-Suite: (a) discuss competitive implications for BuildRight strategy, (b) identify 3–5 strategic actions (e.g., launch private label in category where competitor is strong, increase promotional frequency in region where competitor is expanding, accelerate ecommerce features where competitor is weak), (c) actions integrated into initiative tracker per W1660
Responsible (R): CMO / CEO
Accountable (A): CEO
Duration: 2 hours</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1667_Flow12</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1667_Flow13</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W1667_End7" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W1667_Flow13</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W1667_Annotation8">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-342 (ensure controlled execution — Competitive Intelligence &amp; Market Analysis (PA-33.3).) | - operational: standard operating procedures; system-enforced validation rules
Owner: CMO</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
